course: dictionary
lesson: 9042
title: Slavonic: a word about peoples and languages
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Slavonic is a word with a few meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. Slavonic means to do with the Slavs, the peoples of central and eastern Europe, or with their languages. «The Ostroh Bible of 1581 was the first complete Bible in Church Slavonic» is about a language, because you can print a Bible in a language but not in a people.
explain: Look for clue words. Church tells you that Church Slavonic is linked to church services. Printed and Bible show that the text is in writing. Put these clues together and you can guess that Church Slavonic is an old language, then check it with a dictionary.
explain: The same word can describe other things too. «Dvořák wrote Slavonic Dances» is about music. The Dances are linked to the Slavic peoples, so Slavonic describes their style. Slavonian is a different word, linked to the region of Slavonia in Croatia.
fact: Slavonic is also spelt Slavic. Both mean the same thing.
fact: Ukrainian, Polish and Czech are Slavonic languages, and they are related to each other like English is to German.
fact: Saints Cyril and Methodius created an alphabet for Old Church Slavonic in the 800s.
fact: Slavonia is a region of Croatia, and «Slavonian» describes things from that region.
fact: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, read the sentence around it and choose the meaning that fits.
exercise: «The Ostroh Bible of 1581 was the first complete Bible in Church Slavonic.» What is Church Slavonic? | *An old Slavic language used in church services | A type of church bell | A city in Croatia | A dance from Czech music
exercise: Which three languages are Slavonic languages? | Welsh, Irish and Scots Gaelic | French, Spanish and Italian | Chinese, Japanese and Korean | *Ukrainian, Polish and Czech
exercise: «Dvořák wrote Slavonic Dances.» Is Slavonic here about a language, a dance, or a people? | A region of Croatia | A type of church | A language | *It describes the style of the dances, linked to the Slavs
test: «Slavonian» describes which place? | Scotland | Poland | *Slavonia, a region of Croatia | Ukraine, the country
test: Saints Cyril and Methodius created an alphabet in the 800s for which language? | Welsh | *Old Church Slavonic | Latin | Dances
exam: Read «Prince Kostiantyn Ostrozky founded the Ostroh Academy around 1576.» Slavonic is related to which idea in this lesson? | Wild animals | *Peoples and languages of central and eastern Europe | Mountains in Scotland | Dances only
